  "description": "The shared token file (JSON with client_id, access_token, issued_at, expires_at). input.function write: the SDK's writer stores a login issued at input.issued_at; expected holds the two timestamps as written (YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM:SS+HH:MM: seconds precision, numeric offset, never Z). input.function read: a file holding the given issued_at / expires_at texts, as another SDK may write them; expected holds the instants read, at +05:30, with expires_at capped at the first 06:00 IST after issued_at, or {\"error\": \"invalid\"} when the file is refused. A reader accepts exactly YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM:SS, optionally . and 1 to 9 fraction digits (more than 6 are truncated), then Z, z or +HH:MM / -HH:MM, after trimming surrounding whitespace; every other form (no offset, an offset without a colon, the basic format, a space or lower-case t separator, no seconds, 10 or more fraction digits) is refused, and so is an issued_at more than 5 minutes after the reader's clock (the 2099 case).",
